begin;

create temp table week_content (
  sort_index int, title text, body_text text, carry_line text, with_dad_prompt text,
  with_dad_minutes int, share_prompt text, recap_line text
) on commit drop;

insert into week_content values
  (1, $c$Back in the Matrix$c$, $c$Thursday night you turned your phone off.

For three days nobody could reach you. And somewhere in the quiet, something happened in you. Maybe it was big. Maybe it was small enough you're not sure it counts.

It counts.

This morning the phone is back on. By lunch, the weekend might feel like it happened to somebody else. That doesn't mean it wasn't real. It means you're back in the matrix, and the matrix is loud.

This is where you keep it. A few minutes a day.

Every day there's a short reading and audio from me. They're not the same. The reading reminds you. The audio takes it further. Do both.

Then time with Dad. Not a lesson. A conversation.

You didn't do the weekend alone. Don't do this alone either. Join the alumni group below and tell the guys you're in.$c$, $c$Dad gets the first two minutes.$c$, $c$Phone face down. Ask Him: *Father, what don't You want me to lose from this weekend?* Then be quiet and listen. If something comes, put it in your notes. If nothing comes, that's okay. You showed up.$c$, 2, $c$Join the alumni group. Post your name and which camp you went to.$c$, $c$Camp turned the noise off long enough for you to hear. Now you get to choose the quiet. Dad gets the first two minutes.$c$),
  (2, $c$Something Stirred$c$, $c$Remember how Thursday night started? Before anyone said a word, three trailers played. Braveheart. Saving Private Ryan. Open Range.

And something in you sat up.

Most men won't admit that. It feels a little silly to get stirred up by a movie trailer. But it wasn't the movies. It was you. Something in you wants to fight for something. To go somewhere. To matter.

A lot of good men get to where everything looks fine on paper. And underneath sits a question they never say out loud: *Is this it?*

That question isn't ungrateful. It's a clue. Those desires aren't a defect. God put them there. The glory of God is a man fully alive, not a man who has managed his heart into silence.

This week, notice when it stirs again. A song in the truck. Your kid doing something brave. That's your heart, still alive.

And if nothing stirred this weekend, that's okay. Some hearts have been quiet a long time. That's exactly why you're here.$c$, $c$Smoke means fire.$c$, $c$Ask Him: *Father, what did You stir in me this weekend?* Then listen.$c$, 2, $c$Which trailer got you?$c$, $c$What stirred Thursday night wasn't the movies. It was your heart, and it's alive. Smoke means fire.$c$);

